Sound files for the built-in engine's tests (builtin_test.go), copied as
they are from goframework's own test files (The Free License, as the
framework):

- lame-mono22.mp3: goframework.io/codecs-audio-mp3 testdata at 9b46e67,
  made by its testdata/make.sh: LAME, 32 kbit/s, from one second of a
  signal ffmpeg's aevalsrc computes (tones, a chirp, bursts, a little
  noise) at 22.05 kHz mono. No recording of anyone's.
- ffmpeg-mono22.aac: goframework.io/codecs-audio-aac testdata at bd85214,
  made by its testdata/make.sh: ffmpeg's AAC LC encoder at 32 kbit/s, ADTS,
  from the same kind of signal at 22.05 kHz mono.
- stereo-c1000.ape to stereo-c5000.ape: goframework.io/codecs-audio-ape
  testdata at d58266c, made by its testdata/make.sh: Monkey's Audio 13.46's
  encoder at each level (fast, normal, high, extra high, insane) from 0.6 s
  of the same kind of signal at 44.1 kHz stereo (R101).

The tagged MP3s (ID3v2.2, 2.3, 2.4, ID3v1, a PNG cover) are made by the
tests themselves from lame-mono22.mp3's frames.
